<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smallholder up on good tea prices.</title>
<headline>Tea Smallholder up on good tea prices.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>High tea prices led to small investors pushing up Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd by 2.9 percent or 50 cents to 18 rupees on turnover of 7,000 shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share is liquid, cheap and sound, making it an ideal retail buy,&quot; said a broker specialising in retail trade.</p>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories processes leaf bought from small cultivators. Investors are bullish on the plantation sector and allied shares, due to Sri Lankan tea prices being at near record levels.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
